Triangle T(m,R) (1 <= R <= m) giving shortest possible length n of an [n,n-m] binary linear code with covering radius R.

The 29 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A060451

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
